 to assist in code review in [Chrome](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/codecov/gedikamndpbemklijjkncpnolildpbgo) or Firefox (https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/codecov/)\r\n\r\n*Highly detailed* **pull request comments** and *customizable* **commit statuses** will improve your team's workflow and code coverage incrementally.\r\n\r\n**File backed configuration** all through the `codecov.yml`. \r\n\r\n## FAQ\r\n- Do you **merge multiple uploads** to the same commit? **Yes**\r\n- Do you **support multiple languages** in the same project? **Yes**\r\n- Can you **group coverage reports** by project and/or test type? **Yes**\r\n- How does **pricing** work? Only paid users can view reports and post statuses/comments. ","external_url":"https://codecov.io","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/codecov","created_at":"2016-09-25T14:18:27Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T19:12:59Z","permissions":{"administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"read","emails":"read","issues":"read","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["delete","fork","member","membership","organization","public","pull_request","push","release","repository","status","team_add"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/issues/comments/5294923648","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pull/15680#issuecomment-5294923648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/issues/15680","id":5294923648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCxQENc8AAAABO5ofgA","user":{"login":"blakerouse","id":3869671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4Njk2NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3869671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse","html_url":"https://github.com/blakerouse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blakerouse/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T15:12:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T15:12:30Z","body":"I know we talked about this some in the SIG and I was un-clear why talking about it, if this was truly needed. After more review of this code and change I do believe we should merge this.\r\n\r\nWith `retry_on_failure: false` there is no retrySender, so no errors ever get wrapped as `ShutdownErr`. If a request is in-flight when the collector starts shutting down and the export fails (e.g. the underlying TCP/gRPC connection is torn down as the collector exits), the persistent queue receives a plain error and deletes the request, causing data loss. After a restart the request is gone.\r\n\r\nIf the exporter doesn't error during shutdown, the shutdownSender is a no-op, it only acts on errors. The change is specifically for the race between in-flight requests being drained and the underlying transport closing.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/issues/comments/5294923648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/issues/comments/5460027108","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector/pull/15680#issuecomment-5460027108","issue_url":"https://api.github